        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Cant have a debate about a group without that group in the room. Its unethical and produces false reports. this is standard protocol in research the fact your school even humored it is laughable. but I will say my school didnt even offer a queer theory or womens studies ourse, one professor had the ability to teach it so i asked for a 1 on 1 lecture spot to getthe credits and the school allowed it. It was just me and that teacher for 2 months basically discussing 50 books and me writing dissertations.\n\nthe end thesis I wrote ended with 1 small paragraph boiling down to. \" In light of recent changes in public persception in regards to the current femminist movement and queer bodies to include or not include trans people, It is best for trans women in particular to stay in the closet metaphorically. Out of absolute safety. too many pieces of \"academic\" theory contradict each other now and it is best to transtion with the express purpose of passing 100% with stealth and to only come out to a potential partner and noone else. the LGBTQI comunity cannot be trusted and nor can the cishet comunity.\""
        },
